They worked eight-hour shifts,

191
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:07,180
pulling tons of coal in carts along underground railways.

192
00:13:07,980 --> 00:13:10,040
At their peak use in 1913,

193
00:13:10,041 --> 00:13:14,340
70,000 pit ponies worked underground in Great Britain.

194
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:18,820
The term horsepower was invented by steam engine pioneer James Watt

195
00:13:18,821 --> 00:13:22,520
when he observed how much weight one pit pony could pull.

196
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:28,700
Rather than call it pony power, he increased the test results by 50%

197
00:13:28,701 --> 00:13:30,600
