200
00:13:36,741 --> 00:13:44,220
When wooden plow blades were replaced by metal, horses could pull them through dense, hard-packed

201
00:13:44,221 --> 00:13:47,180
soil more quickly than oxen.

202
00:13:47,181 --> 00:13:53,280
By the mid-18th century, the horse-drawn plow was a farmer's dream machine.

203
00:13:53,281 --> 00:13:58,280
Using hand tools, a man could only till a sixth of an acre per day.

204
00:13:58,281 --> 00:14:00,920
With oxen, maybe a half acre.

205
00:14:00,921 --> 00:14:05,980
But a single horse-drawn plow increased daily production to a full acre.

206
00:14:05,981 --> 00:14:11,580
mechanical farm machinery like this appeared it still needed horsepower.

207
00:14:11,581 --> 00:14:16,700
At the time of the revolution the average family farm might have been a hundred acres.

208
00:14:16,701 --> 00:14:25,500
By 1830, 1840 because of increased machinery, you've got the reaper, you've got all kinds

209
00:14:25,501 --> 00:14:30,620
of sophisticated technology that's starting to come along and it needed a stronger power source.

210
00:14:30,621 --> 00:14:39,400
Just as freeways spawned the development of suburbs today, trails cleared for horses expanded the boundaries of early cities.

211
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:49,620
In the mid-19th century, streets were filled with horses and wagons, from the simple carts of fruit peddlers to fancy carriages.

212
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:57,180
By 1859, 40 manufacturers in New York City were selling 5,000 carriages per year.

213
00:14:57,181 --> 00:15:07,140
By 1900, New York City boasted a population of 150,000 horses, generating 10 million pounds of manure a year.

214
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:11,000
Far more than could be used readily as fertilizer.

215
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:14,300
But then came a godsend for city street sweepers.

216
00:15:15,580 --> 00:15:16,760
The steam engine.

217
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:24,120
When steam and gasoline-powered vehicles became popular and affordable, many workforces were retired.

218
00:15:24,121 --> 00:15:26,500
